  "body": "The parent stack #3472 is merged. This branch is refreshed on the latest `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\nJudge an ordinary axial spot cone at the measured part top.\nUse a separate optional `VerifyContext::rim_top_z` bound for finished hole walls.\nKeep the stock top for rapid and collision checks.\nKeep the nominal cutter radius for invalid caps, lateral feeds, and untrusted cutter geometry.\nOther callers retain the stock-top fallback.\n\nThe synthetic case has a part top at Z12 and a stock top at Z13.\nAn 8 mm, 90-degree spot with its tip at Z10 now verifies and posts.\nIts radius is 2 mm at the part top, inside the 2.5 mm hole radius.\nA spot with its tip at Z9 still gives a gouge warning and blocks posting.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/3451-spot-drill-part-top.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe #3020 cone check measured the radius at the raw stock top.\nStock above the finished part enlarged that radius from 2 mm to 3 mm in this case.\nThe check then reported a finished-wall cut that did not exist.\n\n## Tests\n\nApplication suite `spot_drill_verify`: 4 passed.\n\n- `spot_cone_below_extra_stock_clears_the_part_and_posts`\n- `spot_cone_below_extra_stock_that_cuts_the_part_blocks_post`\n\nVerifier suite `spot_drill_radius`: 11 passed.\n\n- `extra_stock_above_the_part_does_not_enlarge_the_spot_footprint`\n- `a_spot_that_cuts_the_part_wall_still_gouges_below_extra_stock`\n- `nonfinite_part_top_never_clears_the_nominal_radius`\n- `a_part_top_does_not_clear_a_lateral_feed`\n\nParent regression after the refresh: `part_off_saved_before_3452`: 2 passed.\n`a_part_off_saved_before_3452_loads_stale_and_does_not_post` reads `Stale` for the saved unsafe part-off and refuses the post.\n\nReadings on head `f3c19705e`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 686 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 61.5 minutes.\n- `spot_drill_verify`: 4 passed. `spot_drill_radius`: 11 passed.\n- `part_off_saved_before_3452`: 2 passed. `turning_part_kerf`: 6 passed.\n- `example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread`: 1 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 3 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe new application clearance pin failed before the production change with `Gouge { at: 1 }`.\nRestoring `radius.rs` from `main` made the direct clearance pin fail.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\nRestoring `generate.rs` from `main` also made the application pin fail.\nThat mutation added only inert `rim_top_z: None` fields so the new context type compiled.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\n\nThe quick gate and the named pins are green on the refreshed head.\nThe readings are in the review comment of this PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone in this PR after the refresh.\n\nThe stack parent #3472 changed four NC files and two catalog project files.\nThat parent is now on `main`, so this PR has no golden or catalog diff:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/groove_part.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/groove_part.nc`\n- `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.nc`\n- `examples/catalog/turning/groove-part-off/groove-part-off.nc`\n- `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.camproj`\n- `examples/catalog/turning/groove-part-off/groove-part-off.camproj`\n\nThe two `.camproj` files changed the file format and their cached paths.\nThe tool rewrote each whole file: format 73 to format 76, new stamps, and new cached paths.\nThe posted `.nc` of each other operation is byte for byte the same.\n`example_catalog` regenerates and compares it.\nThe cone-thread rough-profile cache changed from 476 moves to 433.\nThe cache differences come from `main` changes after the last catalog regeneration, not from this PR.\n\nNo CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe original QA project and its preceding Face operation were not replayed.\nThe synthetic pin uses a legal R plane at raw stock Z13, with the part top at Z12 and tip at Z10.\nDrill cannot use a tilted operation frame.\nFramed contexts retain their conservative stock cap.\nNo UI window, real control, or machine was used.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThis branch is refreshed on `main`, which now holds #3472.\nThe fork received one refresh from another pass (`d6f3edaa4`).\nThis head (`f3c19705e`) merges that refresh and keeps the tree gated here, which is newer on `main`.\nThe two sides added one assertion to `example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread`.\nBoth assert the part-off reaches Z12. The merge took the stricter `main` form that also checks the feed.\nNo other hunk conflicts.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\nNo heavy lane runs for this PR.\nThe heavy tier is a tool, not a merge condition (#3558).\nThis is a `P3` PR, so it runs no targeted heavy step.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: Spot drills below extra stock now verify against the finished part top; spots that cut a finished hole wall still block posting.\n\nFixes #3451\n",
